# (%tid.x − 32·⌊%tid.x/32⌋)·2^26 stays below 2^31 on all 1024 threads,
# and ptxas stores at param_0 plus it. The range of %tid.x taken with
# its own floor, x = 32·q + r, is that of 0·q + 2^26·r, so mul.lo.s32
# does not leave 32 bits; each term on its own would reach 1023·2^26.
RUN: %ptxroof analyze %fixtures/micro/expanded_rem.ptx | FileCheck "%s"
CHECK: kernel micro_expanded_rem
CHECK: st.global.u32  global store 4 B  warp: 32 sectors (ideal 4)  [67108864 * %tid.x - 2147483648 * ⌊%tid.x/32⌋ + param_0]
